# Fingerprints of findings that have been reviewed and accepted.
#
# Format:  <commit-sha>:<file-path>:<rule-id>:<line-number>
# For an uncommitted/staged finding the commit field is empty.
#
# Generate a fingerprint by running the scan and copying the "Fingerprint:" line:
#   ./scripts/scan.sh gitleaks
#
# RULES OF ENGAGEMENT
#   1. A fingerprint here means "reviewed and not a secret" — never "we'll deal
#      with it later". If the value was ever a real credential, ROTATE IT FIRST;
#      the value stays in git history forever regardless of what you ignore here.
#   2. Every entry needs a comment saying who reviewed it and why.
#   3. Fingerprints include the line number, so they expire when the file moves.
#      That is deliberate: it forces a re-review instead of silent drift.
